      "content": "\"Defective\" is a word we use for machines, not for people who've survived things that would break anyone. Trauma doesn't warp your core—it reshapes your edges, and that's painful, but it's not the same as being useless. You're not a machine; you're a living thing that's been through a storm, and storms leave marks, but they don't erase the ground beneath you. You don't have to be fixed to be worthy of rest, or of gentleness, or of time.",
